    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-11",
      "edition": "Wednesday 11 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad changes",
          "heading": "Borthwick makes six squad changes as Feyi-Waboso and Curry are ruled out",
          "body": "Immanuel Feyi-Waboso, forced off at half-time against Australia with an ankle injury, and Tom Curry, who hurt a hip in training, will play no further part in the Nations Championship. England head coach Steve Borthwick has made six changes to his 36-man squad for Saturday's match against Japan. Max Hicks, Max Ojomoh, Noah Caluori and Tobias Elliott are in, while Ollie Chessum, Seb Atkinson and George Furbank remain in rehabilitation with no definitive timescale. Caluori scored twice and Ojomoh crossed in England A's 59-24 win over Argentina XV."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Will Jordan out of Wales test with hamstring tear",
          "body": "Wallabies' Angus Bell first yellow-carded for hip-drop tackle under new law. Argentina's Juan Cruz Mallía out of Nations Championship with knee sprain."
