      "edition": "Wednesday 11 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad watch",
          "heading": "Jeremy Ward trains with France; Rassie Erasmus says Boks never considered him",
          "body": "Stade Français centre Jeremy Ward has been training with Fabien Galthié's France squad this month, though he only qualifies on residency grounds in 2027. The 30-year-old has said he is open to playing for Les Bleus, and Springboks head coach Rassie Erasmus was asked about the switch ahead of Friday's clash in Paris. Erasmus said South Africa had never really considered Ward for a Springbok squad, and that it would be silly to be upset about South African players representing other countries."
        },
