          "kicker": "Hip-drop ruling",
          "heading": "Angus Bell becomes first player yellow-carded for hip-drop tackle under new law",
          "body": "Bell's yellow came after a TMO review in the stoppage for Immanuel Feyi-Waboso's injury, with referee Pierre Brousset deciding it. World Rugby formally outlawed the hip drop on 1 November, so the card is a first under the new rule. Australia went 19-3 down with 14 men, lost 45-22, and Scotland are next. Feyi-Waboso is ruled out of the rest of England's Nations Championship campaign."
        },
